%% Executive views ALL branches - sequence
%% Sources: apps/web/src/routes/_authenticated/dashboard.tsx (branch selector, parallel fetches),
%%          apps/api/src/index.ts (requireReportPrincipal, resolveReportScope, /api/report/dashboard,
%%          /api/twin, /api/report/summary),
%%          apps/api/src/report/clickhouse-report.ts (queryDashboard, buildDashboardSQL,
%%          buildMachineStateSQL, usageFreshnessOf),
%%          apps/api/src/reporting.ts (redactDashboardDataRevenue, mayViewRevenue)
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Exec as Executive (owner)
    participant Web as Web dashboard
    participant API as LaundryTwin API
    participant Guard as Access guard
    participant CH as ClickHouse
    participant Dwh as Warehouse tables

    Note over Exec,Dwh: 1. The executive asks for every branch

    Exec->>Web: opens /dashboard
    Note over Web: branch filter has no branch selected,<br/>which means tenant-wide
    Exec->>Web: picks a date range (from / to)

    Web->>+API: GET /api/report/dashboard?from&to<br/>(no branchId)
    API->>+Guard: requireReportPrincipal

    alt no grant at all
        Guard-->>API: 403 ACCESS_NOT_GRANTED
        API-->>Web: 403 ACCESS_NOT_GRANTED
        Web-->>Exec: Thai error: access revoked or not granted
    else has grants
        Guard-->>-API: principal + grants

        Note over API,Guard: 2. No branchId is a decision, not an omission

        API->>+Guard: resolveReportScope(branchId = undefined)

        alt owner role
            Guard-->>API: scope = undefined (tenant-wide)
            Note over API,Guard: an owner reading every branch<br/>is the one case that widens scope
        else manager or technician
            Guard-->>API: 400 BRANCH_REQUIRED<br/>or the single granted branch
            Note over API,Guard: a narrower role must name a branch,<br/>so it can never read all of them by accident
        end
        deactivate Guard

        Note over API,Dwh: 3. Three queries in parallel - one round trip

        par Branch list + KPIs
            API->>+CH: buildDashboardSQL(from, to, branchId = '')
            CH->>Dwh: fact_machine_usage + dim_branch + dim_machine
            Dwh-->>CH: per-branch revenue and cycles
            CH-->>-API: rows
        and Machine states for the twin
            API->>+CH: buildMachineStateSQL(from, to, branchId = '')
            CH->>Dwh: argMax(status), max(started_at)<br/>countIf(status IN paid, finished)
            Note over CH: usage_rows counted separately,<br/>so "no rows" and "zero" stay different facts
            Dwh-->>CH: per-machine state rows
            CH-->>-API: states
        and Daily trend
            API->>+CH: buildDashboardTrendSQL(from, to, branchId = '')
            CH->>Dwh: day buckets over the same WHERE
            Dwh-->>CH: daily series
            CH-->>-API: trendRows
        end

        Note over API: 4. Freshness and revenue redaction

        API->>API: usageFreshnessOf(lastActiveAt)<br/>fresh / stale / unavailable
        API->>API: redactDashboardDataRevenue(data, canViewRevenue)

        alt role cannot view revenue
            Note over API: revenue fields are nulled,<br/>never sent and hidden by the UI
        else owner or manager
            Note over API: revenue stays
        end

        API-->>-Web: 200 dashboard + source + availability<br/>+ cycleAttribution
        Note over Web,Exec: source tells the executive<br/>whether this is real warehouse data
    end

    Note over Exec,Dwh: 5. The dashboard also loads the twin and the summary

    Web->>+API: GET /api/twin?from&to (same scope)
    Note over API: same principal, same resolveReportScope
    API->>CH: queryMachineStates(from, to, scope)
    CH-->>API: machines with status + freshness
    API-->>-Web: 200 machines, availability = usage-derived
    Note over Web: no live telemetry: fact_machine_event holds 0 rows,<br/>so Digital Twin state is derived from usage, not telemetry

    Web->>+API: GET /api/report/summary?from&to
    API-->>-Web: Thai executive summary

    Web-->>Exec: KPIs, branch cards, twin grid, summary

    Note over Exec,Dwh: 6. Failure is reported, not faked

    alt analytics source unreachable
        API-->>Web: 503 ANALYTICS_SOURCE_UNAVAILABLE
        Web-->>Exec: Thai message naming the source,<br/>never a zero-filled dashboard
    end
